+### Gaussian Grounded Inter-Reflection
+A technique to model inter-reflection by separating direct light $L_{dir}$ and indirect light $L_{ind}$, approximating visibility $V$ via ray tracing on an extracted mesh to determine occlusion [S5, unofficial].
+**Steps:**
+1. Calculate the reflected direction $R$ for visibility checks: $R = 2(\omega_o \cdot N)N - \omega_o$ [S5, unofficial].
+2. Periodically extract the object's surface mesh during optimization using truncated signed distance function (TSDF) fusion [S5, unofficial].
+3. Perform ray tracing against the extracted mesh using a Bounding Volume Hierarchy (BVH) to accelerate intersection checks and determine visibility $V$ (1 if visible, 0 if occluded) [S5, unofficial].
+4. Assign each Gaussian an additional view-dependent color $l_{ind}$ modeled by spherical harmonics [S5, unofficial].
+5. Evaluate $l_{ind}$ in the reflected direction at the Gaussian level and aggregate the indirect lighting map via alpha-blending: $l_{\text{ind}} = \sum_{i=1}^N l_{\text{ind}} \alpha_i \prod_{j=1}^{i-1} (1 - \alpha_j)$ [S5, unofficial].
+**Formula:**
+The modified specular term $L'_s$ accounts for visibility $V$: $L'_s(\omega_o) \approx \left( \int_{\Omega} f_s(\omega_i, \omega_o) (\omega_i \cdot \mathbf{N}) d\omega_i \right) \cdot [L_{\text{dir}} \cdot V + L_{\text{ind}} \cdot (1 - V)]$ [S5, unofficial].
